{"type":"text","timestamp":1794356917150,"sessionID":"ses_e38045b15ffejDFKnkcMhyDjwn","part":{"id":"prt_1c801b390001vn1lguFMMgxBwH","messageID":"msg_1c800efe3001b6TlDIaURcmGIA","sessionID":"ses_e38045b15ffejDFKnkcMhyDjwn","type":"text","text":"Now I need to fix the PATCH logic — I spotted a bug where the status update wouldn't be applied in the position branch. Rewriting the handlers cleanly:\n\n","time":{"start":1794356917136,"end":1794356917147}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794356917173,"sessionID":"ses_e38045b15ffejDFKnkcMhyDjwn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_27b8e52034e74d32bed2a534","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/tasks.py","newString":"def _column_ids(conn, status: str, exclude_id: int | None = None) -> list[int]:\n    sql = \"SELECT id FROM tasks WHERE status = ?\"\n    params: list = [status]\n    if exclude_id is not None:\n        sql += \" AND id != ?\"\n        params.append(exclude_id)\n    sql += \" ORDER BY position, id\"\n    return [row[\"id\"] for row in conn.execute(sql, params).fetchall()]\n\n\ndef _rebalance(conn, status: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Assign gap-free positions 1..n to all tasks of a column.\"\"\"\n    for offset, task_id in enumerate(_column_ids(conn, status)):\n        conn.execute(\"UPDATE tasks SET position = ? WHERE id = ?\", (offset + 1, task_id))\n\n\ndef _place(conn, ordered_ids: list[int]) -> None:\n    for offset, task_id in enumerate(ordered_ids):\n        conn.execute(\"UPDATE tasks SET position = ? WHERE id = ?\", (offset + 1, task_id))","oldString":"def _column_ids(conn, status: str, exclude_id: int | None = None) -> list[int]:\n    sql = \"SELECT id FROM tasks WHERE status = ?\"\n    params: list = [status]\n    if exclude_id is not None:\n        sql += \" AND id != ?\"\n        params.append(exclude_id)\n    sql += \" ORDER BY position, id\"\n    return [row[\"id\"] for row in conn.execute(sql, params).fetchall()]\n\n\ndef _rebalance(conn, status: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Assign gap-free positions 1..n to all tasks of a column.\"\"\"\n    for offset, task_id in enumerate(_column_ids(conn, status)):\n        conn.execute(\"UPDATE tasks SET position = ? WHERE id = ?\", (offset + 1, task_id))\n\n\ndef _place(conn, status: str, ordered_ids: list[int]) -> None:\n    for offset, task_id in enumerate(ordered_ids):\n        conn.execute(\"UPDATE tasks SET position = ? WHERE id = ?\", (offset + 1, task_id))"}